#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# gegenbauer_c

#% text
# `gegenbauer_c(n, a, x)` gives the Gegenbauer polynomial C_n^(a)(x).

#% text
# `gegenbauer_c(n, x)` gives the limit (2/n) T_n(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At a non-negative integer degree the polynomial is expanded in its argument (evaluated for numbers).

#% item
# At other numeric degrees the hypergeometric representation gives the value; symbolic degrees stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
gegenbauer_c(2, a, x)
#% output
#= -a + 2*a*x^2 + 2*a^2*x^2

#% cell
gegenbauer_c(3, x)
#% output
#= (2/3)*(-3*x + 4*x^3)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
gegenbauer_c(2.5, 1.5, 0.3)
#% output
#= -1.5821725940398246

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `chebyshev_t`, `jacobi_p`
